- Relevance quality ceiling: ts_rank ≠ BM25; no typo tolerance, no infix/prefix matching, no synonyms, no ranking learning. Mitigation ladder: pg_trgm fallback for partial words (v2), the FUSE extension, and then external engines (ADR revisit triggers).
- English-only config hard-coded in the generated column → multilingual workspaces need per-language config / unaccent (unaccent extension + text-search template change = a migration; accepted debt).
- ts_headline CPU at limit=100 (bounded by design R2).
- Relevance-sort cursor instability under concurrent writes (E10, accepted; document: pages may show an edited task twice / skip it — acceptable for search but not for exports; exports are explicitly v2 async jobs).
- Legacy unscoped GET /tasks remains live until deprecated (R6/open follow-up) — risk accepted only for this cycle because it's flagged.
- Sort CASE on priority is not index-friendly; at per-workspace scale it's a memory sort; the documented upgrade is a generated priority_rank column + composite index if p95 shows the sort cost.
