Performance 10k→1M	Both pass to horizon; A wins at this scale	NFR is per workspace (100k). Scope-first filtering + keyset pagination keep per-query work proportional to the slice, not the corpus. A's real risk at 1M is a cross-tenant GIN bitmap scan on broad terms — the ADR documents a measure-first ladder: project_id = ANY(...) semi-join → btree_gin composite (project_id, search_vector) → trigger-denormalized workspace_id (same-DB copy, not an external dual-write).
