Key implementation points (the "how")
- One sort fragment, three uses. sortBy resolves through a server-side allowlist of Prisma.sql fragments spliced identically into SELECT, the keyset WHERE, and ORDER BY — the cursor can't desync from the sort by construction.
- Priority: CASE ... WHEN 'urgent' THEN 4 ELSE 0 END — ELSE 0 also absorbs E12 (unknown stored values sort deterministically, never 500).
- Cursor tiebreaker: row-value comparison (sortExpr, t.id) < (cursorV, cursorId). The subtle bug is that < is three-valued under NULL (ROW(NULL,x) < ROW(1,a) → NULL → rows silently vanish), which breaks paging over NULL dueDate (the only nullable sort key). Fix: COALESCE(due_date, ±'infinity'::timestamptz) — since NULLS LAST means NULL behaves as the order-extreme in both directions, the sentinel maps that semantics exactly onto lexicographic row comparison. The sentinel stays SQL-internal; the cursor token carries the raw v: null.
- page CTE pattern: rank + top-N run on (id, v) only; joins for the E16 embeds and ts_headline snippets run on ≤ limit+1 rows — this is what keeps snippet CPU inside p95. One trap flagged: ts_headline doesn't escape user content, so snippets use custom sentinel delimiters → HTML-escape whole string → swap sentinels for <mark>.
